Relevant columns & their roles for “Sept‑2018 1‑week‑cohort 1, 2, 3‑week retention”  
• `event_name` : filter the cohort seed event (`'first_open'`) and detect any later activity.  
• `event_timestamp` : micro‑seconds UTC – add 8 h to convert to Shanghai local time and decide in‑week / out‑week activity.  
• `event_date` : quick partition filter that matches table suffix; helps restrict reading.  
• `user_pseudo_id` : anonymous GA4 user id – used to build the cohort & count returning users.  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX` (automatic) : lets us wildcard‑query all `events_201809*` tables while reading only the needed dates.  

Typical conditions  
• `event_name = 'first_open'` — seeds the cohort.  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'` — limits tables to 1 – 7 Sept 2018.  
• `TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp+8*60*60*1000000)` BETWEEN '2018‑09‑01' AND '2018‑09‑07 23:59:59' ASIA/SHANGHAI — guarantees Shanghai local time window.  
• `user_pseudo_id IN (…)` — restricts later‑week queries to cohort users only.  

Below are ten exploratory → final BigQuery SQLs (each different, 20‑row LIMIT except the final one).

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek raw rows for 1 Sep 2018.
SELECT *
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180901`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Distinct event names that occurred on 1 Sep 2018.
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180901`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Sample of first_open events on 1–7 Sep (Shanghai local date shown).
SELECT
  user_pseudo_id,
  event_name,
  DATETIME(TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp+8*60*60*1000000), "Asia/Shanghai") AS shanghai_time
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
  AND event_name = 'first_open'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Daily count of first_open during the cohort‑forming week.
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS evt_day,
  COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id) AS new_users
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
  AND event_name = 'first_open'
GROUP BY evt_day
ORDER BY evt_day
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) List 20 cohort user ids (deduped).
SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
  AND event_name = 'first_open'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Check which of those cohort users came back during week‑1 (8–14 Sep).
SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '08' AND '14'
  AND user_pseudo_id IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
        FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
          AND event_name = 'first_open')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Retained user counts by week‑number (1,2,3) without percentages yet.
WITH cohort AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
),
activity AS (
  SELECT
    user_pseudo_id,
    DATE(TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp+8*60*60*1000000),"Asia/Shanghai") AS act_date
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '08' AND '28'
    AND user_pseudo_id IN (SELECT user_pseudo_id FROM cohort)
)
SELECT
  CASE
    WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-08' AND '2018-09-14' THEN 1
    WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-15' AND '2018-09-21' THEN 2
    WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-22' AND '2018-09-28' THEN 3
  END AS week_num,
  COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id) AS retained_users
FROM activity
GROUP BY week_num
ORDER BY week_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Same as #7 but adds cohort size & computes retention rate per week row.
WITH cohort AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
), activity AS (
  SELECT
    user_pseudo_id,
    DATE(TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp+8*60*60*1000000),"Asia/Shanghai") AS act_date
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '08' AND '28'
    AND user_pseudo_id IN (SELECT user_pseudo_id FROM cohort)
)
SELECT
  CASE
    WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-08' AND '2018-09-14' THEN 1
    WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-15' AND '2018-09-21' THEN 2
    WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-22' AND '2018-09-28' THEN 3
  END AS week_num,
  COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id) AS retained_users,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cohort) AS cohort_size,
  COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id)/(SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cohort) AS retention_rate
FROM activity
GROUP BY week_num
ORDER BY week_num
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Pivot the previous output so each week’s retention becomes its own column.
WITH cohort AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
), activity AS (
  SELECT
    user_pseudo_id,
    DATE(TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp+8*60*60*1000000),"Asia/Shanghai") AS act_date
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '08' AND '28'
    AND user_pseudo_id IN (SELECT user_pseudo_id FROM cohort)
), retention AS (
  SELECT
    CASE
      WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-08' AND '2018-09-14' THEN 1
      WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-15' AND '2018-09-21' THEN 2
      WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-22' AND '2018-09-28' THEN 3
    END AS week_num,
    user_pseudo_id
  FROM activity
  GROUP BY week_num, user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cohort) AS cohort_size,
  COUNTIF(week_num=1) / (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cohort) AS week1_retention,
  COUNTIF(week_num=2) / (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cohort) AS week2_retention,
  COUNTIF(week_num=3) / (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cohort) AS week3_retention
FROM retention
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL ANSWER – weekly retention (weeks 1‑3) of users whose first_open happened 1‑7 Sept 2018 (Shanghai time).  No LIMIT applied.
WITH cohort AS (
  -- users whose very first contact is within 1–7 Sep (Shanghai)
  SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '07'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
    AND TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp + 8*60*60*1000000)
        BETWEEN TIMESTAMP('2018-09-01', 'Asia/Shanghai')
            AND TIMESTAMP('2018-09-08', 'Asia/Shanghai')
),
activity AS (
  -- any later activity by cohort users during 8–28 Sep
  SELECT
    user_pseudo_id,
    DATE(TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp + 8*60*60*1000000), 'Asia/Shanghai') AS act_date
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_201809*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '08' AND '28'
    AND user_pseudo_id IN (SELECT user_pseudo_id FROM cohort)
),
retention AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT
    user_pseudo_id,
    CASE
      WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-08' AND '2018-09-14' THEN 1
      WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-15' AND '2018-09-21' THEN 2
      WHEN act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-22' AND '2018-09-28' THEN 3
    END AS week_num
  FROM activity
  WHERE act_date BETWEEN '2018-09-08' AND '2018-09-28'
)
SELECT
  COUNT(*)                                   AS cohort_size,
  COUNTIF(week_num = 1) / COUNT(*) AS week1_retention,
  COUNTIF(week_num = 2) / COUNT(*) AS week2_retention,
  COUNTIF(week_num = 3) / COUNT(*) AS week3_retention
FROM cohort
LEFT JOIN retention
USING (user_pseudo_id);
```

